  "id": "osf-review-parallel-lenses",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-07T10:21:07.073Z",
  "title": "Review lenses run in parallel under time and cost limits",
  "summary": "The reviewer run stops being a sequential loop over lenses. Each lens now runs on a bounded thread pool (default 8 at once), each in its own read-only clean copy of the change, and two new clocks bound it: a per-lens budget that a retry must share, and a whole-run deadline counted from the first lens start. A lens that panics, fails, or runs out of time is recorded as could-not-run with the binding limit named, and the other lenses finish. `[review]` gains `concurrency` and `total_timeout_seconds`, both validated at load, and the per-attempt default rises from 300s to 1800s.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
